  "rules": "CONNECT FOUR - 6 rows x 7 columns, connect 4 to win.\n\nGOAL\nBe the first to get 4 of your own discs in an unbroken straight line: horizontally,\nvertically or diagonally (both diagonal directions count).\n\nBOARD AND PIECES\nThe board is a vertical grid with 6 rows and 7 columns, numbered 1 to 7 from left to right.\nPlayer 0 plays X and moves first; Player 1 plays O. Players alternate, one disc per turn.\nA disc is dropped into a column and falls to the LOWEST empty cell of that column (gravity).\nYou cannot choose the row, and you cannot drop into a full column. Passing is not allowed.\n\nACTION FORMAT\n    drop <column>\nwhere <column> is a number from 1 to 7 of a column that is not full.\nExamples:  \"drop 4\"   \"drop 1\"   \"drop 7\"\nAnything else (a full column, a number out of range, other text) is illegal (first time: a warning\nand the same turn again; second time: you lose the game). The arena also sends the list of legal\nmoves every turn.\n\nWHAT YOU OBSERVE\nThe board drawn in text, top row first, \".\" = empty, with column numbers above and below, plus\nthe move history and the open columns. Example after X dropped in 3 and 4, and\nO dropped in 3:\n 1 2 3 4 5 6 7\n|. . . . . . .|\n|. . . . . . .|\n|. . . . . . .|\n|. . . . . . .|\n|. . O . . . .|\n|. . X X . . .|\n+-------------+\n 1 2 3 4 5 6 7\n\nHOW THE GAME ENDS AND IS SCORED\n- The first player to complete a line of 4 (or longer) wins immediately (score 1, loser 0).\n- If the board fills up (42 discs, the move cap) without a line, the game is a draw\n  (0.5 each).\n",
